---
// /roadmap — what the software does today, what is waiting, and what is next.
//
// Rewritten 2026-09-25 with the founder; a fifth status, "planned", added
// 2026-09-26 for committed work nobody is building yet. The page lists capabilities, never
// tasks: no issue links, commands, routes or version numbers. Every "available"
// item was checked against the engine and core repositories that day. The rule
// the page holds itself to: no item is written in the grammar of a stronger
// claim than it can support, and nothing that is not built carries a date.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import OurRoadmap from "../components/Roadmap.astro";
import data from "../data/roadmap.json";

const updated = new Date(`${data.updated}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
  day: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
});

const title = "Roadmap: what is built, waiting and next | Odal Node";
const description =
  "What the Odal Node software does today, what is built and waiting on a legal step, what is in progress, what is planned, and what is being considered. No dates on anything unbuilt.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Section eyebrow="Roadmap" title="What is built, what is waiting, and what comes next." wide>
    <p>
      This page lists capabilities, not tasks, and it is checked against the
      software itself rather than against its own last version.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Nobody is running this in production.</strong> No customers, no
      pilots, no live deployments, and nothing below should be read as evidence
      of any. The battery passport obligation begins on 18 February 2027, and we
      would rather be correct when it arrives than early and wrong.
    </p>
    <p>
      There are no dates on anything unbuilt. Timing depends on EU acts,
      standards votes and registry access, none of which we control, so the
      status is the commitment and a quarter would be a guess.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500">
      Last updated <time datetime={data.updated}>{updated}</time>.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Status" title="Five statuses, never mixed." tone="muted" wide>
    <div class="not-prose">
      <OurRoadmap />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="How items move" title="What it takes to change status." wide>
    <p>
      An item is <strong>available</strong> when it is in a released version
      and a test exercises it through the running system. Merged is not
      available, and neither is demonstrated.
    </p>
    <p>
      An item is <strong>waiting on a legal step</strong> when it is built and
      tested but cannot yet do the thing it exists for, for a legal reason
      rather than an engineering one.
    </p>
    <p>
      An item is <strong>in progress</strong> only while someone is building
      it. An item is <strong>planned</strong> when we have committed to it and
      nobody is building it yet; it carries no date. An item{" "}
      <strong>being considered</strong> is an option: it carries no date and
      no promise.
    </p>
    <p>
      Items can move backwards. Finding out while building something that it
      needs more groundwork is an ordinary outcome, and a reversal recorded here
      is better than an item quietly drifting.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="More detail" title="Where the technical detail lives." tone="tinted" wide>
    <p>
      This page is written for everyone. How each capability works, and how to
      run it, is in the{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.odal-node.io" rel="noopener">documentation</a>, and
      the code itself is{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/odal-node" rel="noopener">public on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>
